3. INDIVIDUAL CONTRIBUTIONS

Amethys Launcher welcomes voluntary contributions from individuals. A person
who proposes code must understand that the purpose of the contribution is to
help build Amethys Launcher, not to obtain individual ownership of the
integrated project code.

Submission, review, discussion, or a public acknowledgement does NOT by itself
transfer copyright or grant permission to incorporate a contribution. Before
any copyrightable individual contribution is merged, distributed, or
incorporated, the contributor must expressly accept and sign a separate
written agreement identifying that specific contribution.

Under that agreement, and only to the extent the contributor owns or is
authorized to transfer the rights, the contributor assigns to Likounsee the
specified transferable economic rights needed to maintain, modify, integrate,
distribute and exploit the accepted contribution as part of Amethys Launcher.
The agreement must specify the contribution and the rights, purpose,
territory, duration and consideration as required by applicable law. It does
not cover future work that is not specifically identified.

Once a valid assignment takes effect, the contributor may not claim ownership
or control of the economic rights assigned. The contributor will be credited
in CONTRIBUTORS.md, with file or feature attribution where reasonably
practicable. Credit recognises the person's work; it does not reverse a valid
assignment. Moral rights and other rights that cannot legally be transferred
or waived remain unaffected.

No contribution may be merged before the agreement is signed by both parties,
the source and rights declarations have been reviewed, and the maintainer has
accepted the contribution. Until then, the contributor retains their rights
and the project may use the material only as needed to review the proposal.

4. CONTRIBUTOR RECOGNITION AND PLANNED REWARDS

The project intends, after completion of Amethys Launcher including its Store
and integrated wallets, to operate a gift-card reward programme for eligible
contributors. The intention is to recognise accepted work and involvement.
Assessment may take account of the amount, complexity, quality, reliability,
regularity and project impact of contributions.

The programme's eligibility rules, assessment process, available budget,
gift-card types, values and distribution conditions must be published before
awards are determined. This statement does not promise a specific value,
recipient, payment date or unconditional reward. Any award is separate from
the rights assignment and does not change ownership of assigned code.

